course: dictionary
lesson: 6628
title: Noticeable and the power of "-able"
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Noticeable means easy to see, hear or notice. If something is noticeable, people spot it without having to search for it. «Winter feeding helps small birds survive, because a small bird can lose a noticeable part of its weight keeping warm.» The bird loses enough weight that anyone measuring it would easily see the change.
explain: A noticeable change is big enough for people to notice. «Natural gas has no smell, so a strong-smelling chemical is added to make leaks noticeable.» Companies want a leak to be easy to spot, so they add a smell. Check your meaning by swapping in "easy to spot" and reading the sentence again.
explain: Phrases often use this word: "a noticeable difference", "barely noticeable" and "clearly noticeable". Barely noticeable means you can only just spot it. Clearly noticeable means anyone could spot it at once.
fact: Noticeable means easy to see, hear or notice.
fact: A noticeable change is big enough for people to notice.
fact: Phrases to learn: "a noticeable difference", "barely noticeable", "clearly noticeable".
fact: Spelling: before -able the final e usually drops (adore, adorable), but it stays after a soft c or g: notice, noticeable.
fact: The comparative is more noticeable, and the superlative is most noticeable.
exercise: «Natural gas has no smell, so companies add a smelly chemical to make leaks noticeable.» What does noticeable mean here? | Expensive to buy | Very quiet | *Easy to smell and spot | Hidden under the ground
exercise: Which spelling is correct? | noticeabel | *noticeable | noticeble | noticable
exercise: «A small bird can lose a noticeable part of its weight keeping warm.» What does noticeable part suggest? | A part that is hard to find | A feather that has fallen out | A part so tiny nobody could weigh it | *A part big enough to notice
test: Which phrase means you can only just spot a change? | *Barely noticeable | Clearly noticeable | Most noticeable | Very loud
test: Which is the comparative form of noticeable? | noticer | *more noticeable | noticeabler | noticeablest
exam: Which meaning fits best in "a noticeable scar on his cheek"? | Sweet smelling | Very old | *Easy to see | Quietly moving
